{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1551076-anyone-disappointed-at-the-lack-of-ixoi-ksirafai-introduction","id":1551076,"title":"Anyone disappointed at the lack of Ixoi/Ksirafai introduction?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-16T11:08:26-07:00","id":1551076,"title":"Anyone disappointed at the lack of Ixoi/Ksirafai introduction?","content":"So, the Razors are well and hale. They never abandoned the Union, but at the present all we have gotten is a bit of tantalizing adumbration. Practically only thing we know certain is that they are loyal and powerful and actively hunting Nephandi in and out of the Union. We know next to nothing about their more recent history, assets, recruitment, organization, focus, paradigm etc.<br /> <br /> I hope against hope to see a dedicated Ksirafai convention book somewhere in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T21:15:46-07:00","id":1551093,"title":"","content":"I would point you to two resources, found in Storyteller's Vault: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/458587/paradigm-explored-eris-enigma\" target=\"_blank\">Paradigm Explored: Eris and Enigma</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/486515/the-book-of-spheres-magicks-disparate-mad\" target=\"_blank\">Book of Spheres: Magicks Disparate and Mad</a>. Both of these products include write-ups of the Ixoi/Ksirafai; and as a bonus, both also give treatments of the Sphere of Telos. The former treats it as a <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/388362/book-of-fragments\" target=\"_blank\">Minor Sphere</a> practiced by the Ksirafai, while the latter treats it as an Entropy variant practiced by the Ixoi. Neither treats it as &quot;The Tenth Sphere&quot;, though both mention that if the Storyteller wants, he can juice it up to serve that role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T09:33:55-07:00","id":1551160,"title":"","content":"I take that there has been news about them in recent OP books, such as the new Guide of the Technocracy?<br /> <hr /><br /> My knowledge about them can be summed as:<br /> <br /> The Ksirafai were a group of occultist assasins that acted as the secret police of the OoR (that were secretly the Ixoi, an ancient greek mystery cult named after the assasin, with a legacy of fighting Nephandi kings, they believe in Telos as the 10 Sphere and that Ascencion it's Armaggedon, and seek to prevent any mage faction to dominate them all - which kinda makes them traitorous to everyone from the get go, albeit this last part was so secret not even the Ksirafai themselves knew, for the most part)<br /> <br /> Then the Technocracy came, and the Ksirafai faked their death and divided their assets between the Union (NWO?) and the OOH (Janissaries), and the only ones that know the truth were Caeron Mustai and some vague something about a hidden library or archive. I was never very clear on how much the Technocracy were aware of the Ksirafai, or how many were still part of the Union - apparently quite a lot.<br /> <br /> Janissaries mantained ties with their Technocracy counterparts, and because of this connection they were executed by the Eutanatoi when the Orphic Circle delated them - this purge came as a suprise to even many Eutanatoi, since it was totally out of order (because of the Horizon War and Storm, the Council wasn't exactly alive, nor were there any general Tradition's body with the authority to issue such an extreme command, AFAIK).<br /> <br /> My pet theory (feeded by some doubts expressed in some books) was that this was another self-purgue, because the Euthanatoi that were responsible were <i>also </i>a secretive cult of assasins powered by greek mythology (who fit the Faction Paradigm very well). And this headcanon was kinda-but-not-really reivindicated by the masked lider of the Golden Chalice being <s>old man jenkins</s> Caeron on one end world scenario...<br /> <br /> Does this hold up?<br /> <hr /><br /> To some extent, I like the way they're an urban legend within legends. An enigma that act as a conspiracy within a conspiracy. And that does require some level of obscurity, a secret it's not a secret if everything it's know about it. But, yeah, I wish there was a bit more about them. Maybe more a &quot;book of conspiracies&quot; than a book about them specificaly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T02:31:26-07:00","id":1551181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> focus, paradigm etc. </div> </div> </div>This is in <i>Technocracy Reloaded</i>. They're basically just highly-trained Black Suits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I take that there has been news about them in recent OP books, such as the new Guide of the Technocracy? </div> </div> </div>In <i>Technocracy Reloaded,</i> there's a mention of a subgroup of Black Suits called the 'Black Daggers'. It's mentioned that other NWO members suspect they might be the Ksirafai.<br /> <br /> <i>The Operative's Dossier</i> has an in-character description that confirms they're the Ksirafai.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T06:44:09-07:00","id":1551190,"title":"","content":"It's neat that the Ksirafai that remained in the Union get a mention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-23T14:28:12-07:00","id":1551247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1551076-anyone-disappointed-at-the-lack-of-ixoi-ksirafai-introduction?p=1551181#post1551181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is in <i>Technocracy Reloaded</i>. They're basically just highly-trained Black Suits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In <i>Technocracy Reloaded,</i> there's a mention of a subgroup of Black Suits called the 'Black Daggers'. It's mentioned that other NWO members suspect they might be the Ksirafai.<br /> <br /> <i>The Operative's Dossier</i> has an in-character description that confirms they're the Ksirafai.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I read them all. And &quot;enhanced black suits&quot; is basically everything what I've gotten. Are you truly thinking that &quot;enhanced black suits&quot; do represent and exhaust everything of modern Ksirafai?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.th