postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1551076-anyone-disappointed-at-the-lack-of-ixoi-ksirafai-introduction?p=1551258#post1551258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sure they could come up with something of they wanted, but as presented so far? Yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, it is disappointing and depressing.<br /> <br /> So I reject it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T19:13:54-08:00","id":1558036,"title":"","content":"Honestly? The New World Order came more or less or of nowhere after the Gabrielites were driven out. I have no problem with the idea that the Ksirafai helped establish the NWO and secretly operate within it. They don't really strike me as the type that would want the attention that would come with being a full-on Convention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-31T03:10:56-08:00","id":1558041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1551076-anyone-disappointed-at-the-lack-of-ixoi-ksirafai-introduction?p=1558035#post1558035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah,</div> </div> </div> </div>That's incredibly dismissive. Especially seeing as you waited over half a year to say anything.<br /> <br /> You asked my opinion. If you want to state your own opinion, go ahead, but don't tell me my own opinion is wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...it is disappointing and depressing. </div> </div> </div>No it's not. It's good actually. A bunch of quasi-Hermetics running around in the modern Technocracy would be awful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I reject it. </div> </div> </div>Good for you. I look forward to reading your brilliant contribution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-05T01:13:00-07:00","id":1559782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1551076-anyone-disappointed-at-the-lack-of-ixoi-ksirafai-introduction?p=1558041#post1558041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's incredibly dismissive. Especially seeing as you waited over half a year to say anything.<br /> <br /> You asked my opinion. If you want to state your own opinion, go ahead, but don't tell me my own opinion is wrong.<br /> <br /> No it's not. It's good actually. A bunch of quasi-Hermetics running around in the modern Technocracy would be awful.<br /> <br /> Good for you. I look forward to reading your brilliant contribution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many apologizes for disrespectful comment. I think you are right and I am wrong. Ksirafai has almost nothing to add to the modern NWO.<br /> <br /> Elaborating on the FIS may be the far better angle to be explored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T23:01:42-07:00","id":1559981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1551076-anyone-disappointed-at-the-lack-of-ixoi-ksirafai-introduction?p=1558036#post1558036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly? The New World Order came more or less or of nowhere after the Gabrielites were driven out. I have no problem with the idea that the Ksirafai helped establish the NWO and secretly operate within it. They don't really strike me as the type that would want the attention that would come with being a full-on Convention.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree the Ksirafai helping form the New World Order is logically consistent, and probably what happened, I find it disappointing.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm just a bit too married to their &quot;quasi-Hermetic assassin cult&quot; aesthetic from Sorcerer's Crusade. But I think it kind of dilutes what the Ksirafai were about - and their distinct appeal - when their &quot;modern incarnation&quot; is functionally indistinguishable from the regular NWO (except with additional dagger imagery).<br /> <br /> At that point, it's not really &quot;the Ksirafai survived into modern day&quot;, but rather &quot;this is an easter egg that goes no deeper than a name check&quot;. Not unless the Black Daggers perform weird rituals involving masks and daggers when the rest of the Union isn't looking.<br /> <br /> At least House Janissary kind of FELT like you were playing Hermetic Mages in a mode distinct from every other OoH House. You could really buy that it's the Ksirafai blending in with the Hermetics, but maintaining their own identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T23:57:14-07:00","id":1559983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1551076-anyone-disappointed-at-the-lack-of-ixoi-ksirafai-introduction?p=1559981#post1559981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think it kind of dilutes what the Ksirafai were about</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends what you think the core of the convention was. Is it the Hermetic-murder cult angle or the secret police angle? Like, personally I think it reads like they adopted a quasi-Hermetic style out of pure practicality, in the same way the wider Order used the seeing stones. There are times that it helps to have an exception to the normal rules. But as time goes on, they become less and less useful, and more and more a liability when interacting with other members of the Order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T06:30:48-07:00","id":1559987,"title":"","content":"The aesthetics of masks + daggers + black swits, w/o magick rituals, gives me a &quot;phantom thief&quot; vive. And there's not much of that on Mage, so they could be it.<br /> <br /> It would be ironic considering the NWO historically comes in part from the Skeleton Keys detectives - &quot;scotland yard&quot;-esque. But, even then, there's often a plot point on &quot;phantom-thief&quot; stories where the &quot;main detective&quot;, that's the only man always seeing the hand of the criminal, it's thus suspected to be working with the criminal - so it wouldn' be completely off key.<br /> <br /> And wouldn't be the first time the Technocracy plays both sides, crime and law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}